ectly, bypassing _run.","Only acli.py:435 (search_issues), acli.py:679 (get_comments), and acli_graph.py self._run sites route through _run."],"finding":"The plan threads the captured jira_cli_timeout only through AcliClient._run, but the primary Cloud operation paths (CREATE via acli_cli_ops.create_issue/_create_from_json_payload, UPDATE via module-level acli.update_issue line 211, add_comment, get_issue, delete_issue line 737) call acli_subprocess._run_acli directly and bypass _run, so they keep resolving reconciler.jira_cli_timeout ambiently — the operation-scoped capture the ticket says it is 'completing' would cover only searches/reads/graph ops, not writes.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f22c20cb4560fbebf","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach bullets 2-3 (AcliClient._run forwarding; _run_acli call_timeout fallback)","norm_id":"nc71dac86c7dc8906","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An operator sets [tool.rebar.reconciler].jira_cli_timeout expecting the whole reconcile pass to honor it; CREATE/UPDATE/DELETE/COMMENT subprocess calls silently keep using the ambient resolve instead of the captured scope value.","A test asserts the captured timeout is honored via _build_cloud but a create/comment write still consults _acli_call_timeout()."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","bl